# Energy flow through a pumping station

The power that reaches the water is worked out from the flow and the head, then traced back
through the pump and the motor to the electrical input. The Sankey diagram draws each flow with
a width in proportion to its power, in kW.

## Inputs
Q: 0.1 m³/s | flow
H_s: 24 m | static lift
H_f: 8 m | friction head in the pipeline
eta_p: 0.78 | pump efficiency
eta_m: 0.93 | motor efficiency
rho: 1000 kg/m³ | water
g: 9.81 m/s²

## Powers
P_static: rho * g * Q * H_s -> kW | lifting the water
P_friction: rho * g * Q * H_f -> kW | lost to pipe friction
P_water: P_static + P_friction -> kW | hydraulic power
P_shaft: P_water / eta_p -> kW | pump shaft
P_in: P_shaft / eta_m -> kW | electrical input
eta: P_static / P_in -> % | useful share of the input

```mermaid
sankey-beta
Electrical input,Motor,43.28
Motor,Motor losses,3.03
Motor,Pump shaft,40.25
Pump shaft,Pump losses,8.86
Pump shaft,Water,31.39
Water,Static lift,23.54
Water,Pipe friction,7.85
```
